# NOTES
# Tooling constraint: all four research passes exhausted WebSearch quota mid-task and hit repeated 403s on NRC.gov/ADAMS FSAR PDFs, the strongest primary source for turbine_supplier and rpv_manufacturer fields. Those two fields are UNVERIFIABLE for most plants as a direct result — this reflects a source-access gap, not necessarily that the claimed values are wrong.
# Recurring confirmed pattern (the "NSSS-vendor-as-constructor" trap named in the task): constructor was WRONG wherever it merely repeated the reactor vendor's name (GE, Westinghouse, CE, B&W) instead of the actual AE/construction firm, for: Shoreham, Susquehanna, Turkey Point, Vermont Yankee, Vogtle 1/2/3/4, Waterford, Watts Bar, Wolf Creek. Recommend auditing this field across the full database, not just this batch.
# South Texas Project: constructor/AE changed mid-construction (Brown & Root 1975-1981 -> Bechtel/Ebasco Constructors 1981-1982 onward). The DB schema has no way to represent a construction-phase handoff; flagging structurally rather than picking one name.
# Surry rpv_manufacturer: input data hedges with "Rotterdam Dockyard / Babcock & Wilcox" — could not resolve which (if either) is correct; no source distinguishes Unit 1 vs Unit 2. Marked UNVERIFIABLE rather than picking one arbitrarily.
# Watts Bar Unit 2: RPV manufacturer for Unit 2 (completed 2016, decades after Unit 1's 1970s-80s original construction) could not be confirmed as either matching Unit 1's original-era fabricator or a distinct later one — flagged as the single most consequential open question in this batch given the multi-decade construction gap.
# Wolf Creek and Susquehanna turbine/rpv fields and Vogtle 3/4 turbine field rest solely on power-technology.com (the flagged last-resort source known to blur NSSS-vendor vs actual fabricator) — recommend a follow-up pass with NRC ADAMS access to upgrade or overturn these LOW-confidence calls.
# Vogtle 3&4 architect_engineer: the modern AP1000 build had a multi-phase contractor history (Shaw Group -> CB&I -> Westinghouse -> Bechtel as EPC from 2017) with no source cleanly naming a single "architect-engineer" of record distinct from the EPC contractor; marked UNVERIFIABLE rather than forcing a fit to the historical AE/constructor/turbine/RPV schema built for 1970s-80s plants.
